            <ArticleTitle>Perinatal diagnosis and management of oropharyngeal fetus in fetu: A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/jcu.22528</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fetus in fetu is an extremely rare congenital anomaly. We describe the perinatal diagnosis and management of a fetus with oropharyngeal and cervical fetus in fetu. High-resolution ultrasonography with 3-dimensional rendering can identify increased risks of airway obstruction in utero. Early identification allows a multidisciplinary team to be assembled for a scheduled ex utero intrapartum treatment procedure. © 2017 Wiley Periodicals, Inc. J Clin Ultrasound, 2017.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2017 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
